# binaries
/bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
/dist/
# go
/vendor/
# anacrolix/torrent's default piece-completion cache: created wherever a test
# builds a real torrent.Client without an explicit storage dir (11.5's
# internal/engine/torrent_live_test.go does, deliberately, to exercise gopeed's
# bt.Fetcher against a real swarm) - not something this repo's own code names
# or controls, so ignoring it here is the fix rather than a code change.
# Both names, because the library renamed it: a run of the current pin leaves
# .torrent.db behind, and the older .torrent.bolt.db is kept so an older
# checkout does not start showing one either.
# The -shm/-wal suffixes are SQLite's own side files: the same run that leaves
# the database leaves those two next to it, and ignoring only the database is a
# rule that catches one of the three files it was written for.
*.torrent.bolt.db*
.torrent.db*
# local/tmp
/tmp/
.DS_Store

# node
node_modules/
web/node_modules/

# Everything scripts/desktop.mjs has Wails generate on every build: the Windows
# manifest and version resource, the macOS Info.plist and icon, the
# installer's helper macros and the WebView2 bootstrapper it carries, and the
# build output. What is committed is what Wails cannot write for us: the icons
# gen-appicon.mjs draws, the build configuration and the installer script.
desktop/build/*
!desktop/build/appicon.png
!desktop/build/appicon.ico
!desktop/build/config.yml
!desktop/build/windows/
desktop/build/windows/*
!desktop/build/windows/nsis/
desktop/build/windows/nsis/*
!desktop/build/windows/nsis/project.nsi
desktop/*.syso
# A signing key never belongs in here. mobile/.gitignore already covers *.jks
# for the app; this is the same rule at the root, because the one place a
# keystore actually gets dropped by accident is next to whatever command was
# being run at the time.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx

# Chrome writes a compiled copy of an extension's declarativeNetRequest
# rulesets into the extension directory it loads, INSIDE the source tree, the
# first time it indexes them. It is a cache, it is stale the moment the rules
# change, and it cost an afternoon: two loads of what looked like the same
# extension behaved differently because one of them was still answering from
# this file. Never commit it, never ship it in the store package.
extension/src/_metadata/

# MkDocs build output; the Docs workflow builds it fresh.
/site/
